          body: "Expect the colour question (black — debride; yellow — debride and absorb; red — protect and moisten; pink — leave alone), the exudate-to-dressing match (dry — hydrogel; heavy — alginate under foam), the sterile-field rules (2.5 cm border, below the waist, wet through), the cleansing direction (clean to dirty, centre out, one swab one stroke), the solution question (warm saline or potable water — not peroxide or Eusol), the 48-hour rule for a closed incision, the Levine swab, and the infection-versus-inflammation timing. Expect suture timings by site and the pull-towards-the-wound rule; evisceration first aid (warm saline pads, supine, knees flexed, nil by mouth, call); drain facts (below the wound, release vacuum before removal, report fresh blood or bile); and the compartment syndrome scenario — pain on passive stretch with a present pulse — answered by splitting the cast to the skin, heart-level elevation and an urgent call, never by more analgesia and a recheck in an hour.",
